  "recipe": {
    "technique": "There are many hundreds of different knitting stitches used by knitters. A piece of knitting begins with the process of casting on, which involves the initial creation of the stitches on the needle. Different methods of casting on are used for different effects: one may be stretchy enough for lace, while another provides a decorative edging.  Provisional cast-ons are used when the knitting will continue in both directions from the cast-on."
